  "sources": {
    "siteClasses": "GB 50011-2010 4.1.6 (site classes by the equivalent shear wave speed and the cover thickness) and Table 5.1.4-2 (Tg by design earthquake group); siteClasses is the chosen group's row (spectrumType, set by the town: locations spectrumType)",
    "spectrumType": "SAEngine practice: a custom location takes design earthquake group 3 (the longest Tg, on the safe side) until the project overrides seismic.spectrumType",
    "minimumScale": "GB 50011 has no scaling of the response spectrum to the static base shear (0); its minimum shear λ (Table 5.2.5) is applied to the static base shear only",
    "pgaFactor": "GB 50011 5.1.5: αmax = 2.25 × the peak ground acceleration (a_h = αmax / 2.25)",
    "orthogonalShare": "GB 50011 5.2.3: √(Sx² + (0.85 Sy)²); SAEngine's 100 % + 85 % is on the safe side",
    "lateralForce.correction": "GB 50011 5.2.1: Geq = 0.85 GE of buildings of more than one storey",
    "lateralForce.minimumShare": "GB 50011 Table 5.2.5: λ of structures with T1 below 3.5 s (0.008, 0.016 (0.024), 0.032 (0.048), 0.064), taken for every period (on the safe side; T1 above 5 s takes 75 %); GB applies it to every storey's shear, SAEngine to the base shear of the static method",
    "liveShare": "GB 50011 5.1.3: 0.5 of the floor live load in the representative gravity load (0.8 for storage and libraries: not applied)",
    "accidentalEccentricity": "GB 50011 5.2.3 / JGJ 3 4.3.3: 5 % of the plan dimension",
    "torsionIrregular": "GB 50011 Table 3.4.3-1: torsional irregularity above 1.2 × the mean storey drift",
    "torsionExtreme": "GB 50011 3.4.4: at most 1.5",
    "torsionAmplificationMax": "GB 50011 has no amplification Ax of the accidental torsion (1.0)",
    "verticalFactor": "GB 50011 5.3: the vertical earthquake of 8 and 9 degree long spans and 9 degree tall buildings is not covered (0)",
    "rareDrift.yieldStrengthRatio": "SAEngine practice: ξy = 0.5 for every storey (the storeys' yield shears are not computed: enter the lowest storey's ξy; GB 5.5.4 also takes 1.5 ηp for a storey whose ξy is below 0.8 of its neighbours' mean)",
    "rareDrift.zones": "GB 50011 5.5.2: required for frames of 7-9 degree with ξy below 0.5 (and others listed there), recommended for the rest: SAEngine checks every 7-9 degree site",
    "rareDrift.defaultAmplification": "GB 50011 5.5.3: the simplified method holds for frames up to 12 storeys; others take ηp 2.2 here (SAEngine practice) and should be checked by pushover or time history",
    "gradeDesign.adjustment": "GB 50011-2010 Table 5.4.2: γRE beams 0.75, columns 0.75 (μN < 0.15) / 0.80, shear walls 0.85, shear and members in eccentric tension 0.85; steel members strength 0.75, stability 0.80 (the columns' 0.80 for every column: P)",
    "seismicGrades.detailing": "GB 50011-2010 6.3.3 (beam ends x/h0 <= 0.25 / 0.35, As'/As >= 0.5 / 0.3, Table 6.3.3 hoop zone max(2 hb, 500) / max(1.5 hb, 500), hoops min(hb/4, 6 d / 8 d, 100 / 150), dia 10 / 8 / 8 / 6), GB 50010-2010 Table 11.3.6-1 (beam steel at the supports 0.40 % and 80 ft/fy ... span 0.30 % and 65 ft/fy ...), GB 50011 Table 6.3.7-1 (column steel %, frame structures in brackets, + 0.05 for 400 MPa bars, + 0.1 below), Table 6.3.7-2 (hoops min(6 d / 8 d, 100 / 150) mm, dia 10 / 8 / 8 / 6; 三, 四 base 100 mm not told apart), 6.3.9 (zone max(hc, Hn/6, 500), ρv >= λv fc/fyv, fc at least of C35, ρv >= 0.8 / 0.6 / 0.4 / 0.4 %, Table 6.3.9 λv of ordinary and compound hoops), 6.4.3 (wall webs 0.25 % / 0.20 % for 四); every value U",
    "seismicGrades.anchorage": "GB 50010-2010 11.1.7: ζaE 1.15 (一, 二), 1.05 (三), 1.00 (四)",
    "verticalComponent": "GB 50011-2010 5.3.3: the vertical action of long spans and cantilevers 10 % (8, 0.20g), 15 % (8, 0.30g), 20 % (9) of the representative gravity load; GB 55002-2021 4.3.2 γEv 0.5 with the horizontal action (U); 5.3.1 (FEvk = 0.65 αmax × 0.75 GE of 9-degree tall buildings) not computed: the 20 % share taken (U); the dead load stands for the representative gravity load (P); the response spectrum combinations only (the static earthquake rows have no Ev)",
    "lateralForce.topForce": "GB 50011-2010 5.2.1, Table 5.2.1: δn = 0.08 T1 + 0.07 (Tg <= 0.35), + 0.01 (0.35-0.55), - 0.02 (> 0.55) where T1 > 1.4 Tg; ΔFn = δn FEk at the top, the rest (1 - δn) FEk by Gi Hi; δn at most 0.9 (P)"
  }
